[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2871364803","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106257#issuecomment-2871364803","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106257","id":2871364803,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rJYzD","user":{"login":"lodetrick","id":146759331,"node_id":"U_kgDOCL9eow","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146759331?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick","html_url":"https://github.com/lodetrick","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-12T08:17:56Z","updated_at":"2025-05-12T23:32:09Z","body":"Ok, I took a deeper look at how the `tab_separation` worked and realized that we should just always use the `ofs_cache` when drawing the tabs, we don't need to recalculate it and add more redundant code. I realized that a lot of the if statements were bandaid fixes that could be removed once the ofs_cache was correct. This ended up cleaning the code related to the `tab_separation` a lot, removing all but five instances of the variable in the code while still acting the same.\r\n\r\nKnown: Issue with clipping tabs that clips them at the wrong positions, looking into it. (Fixed)\r\nKnown: Same issue with interleaved hidden tabs but when dragging tabs, looking into it. (Fixed)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2871364803/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2874587418","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106257#issuecomment-2874587418","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106257","id":2874587418,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rVrka","user":{"login":"lodetrick","id":146759331,"node_id":"U_kgDOCL9eow","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146759331?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick","html_url":"https://github.com/lodetrick","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-12T23:47:08Z","updated_at":"2025-05-12T23:48:02Z","body":"Alright, here's what I did:\r\n\r\nI reworked how it calculates where to place the dropping texture (the bar that shows up between tabs).  Instead of calculating the average distance between tabs one apart, it merely adds and subtracts half the `tab_separation`, which is defined to be the distance between tabs. This removed a rather complicated bundle of if-statements and made the code structure closer to how it was before `tab_separation` was implemented.\r\n\r\nI took the opportunity to add the `get_previous_available` and `get_next_available` public methods (making the `select_previous_available` use these internally), these methods are really useful in cases where there are hidden tabs interleaved. Bringing it back to #106164, these methods are necessary for the functionality to move tabs using buttons through the dock manager popup, as the bottom dock is structured to have interleaved hidden tabs. There are no docs for these yet, if this passes checks and is not urgent then I'll let a future PR decide if we want to expose these methods.\r\n\r\nI also reworked the `get_closest_tab_idx_to_point` method. Previously it used the Vector2.distance function but since the TabBar only works on an axis we can just compute `abs(tab_center.x - p_point.x)`. This is an easy performance increase, and if vertical tabs are implemented we only need to change the axis.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2874587418/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2880538373","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106257#issuecomment-2880538373","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106257","id":2880538373,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rsYcF","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-14T14:50:14Z","updated_at":"2025-05-14T14:50:14Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2880538373/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":2,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]